{"id":"int-2680e61e870a2aee887a32215adec820","kind":"field_change","created_at":"2026-05-31T23:53:43.908288Z","actor":"Mike","issue_id":"nullpipe-2fe","extra":{"field":"status","new_value":"closed","old_value":"open","reason":"Fix invite command deadlock: host_with_client_inner wrapped Hub in Arc<tokio::sync::Mutex> but hub.run() holds the lock forever (accept loop never returns until shutdown). All command handlers (invite, peers, send, quit) tried to lock the same mutex — permanent deadlock.\n\nFix: Don't wrap Hub in Arc<Mutex>. Extract shared state (address, peers Arc<PeerRegistry>, broadcast_tx) before handing Hub ownership to the background task. Use a watch channel for shutdown signaling instead of locking the hub."}}
